[Music]  vladimir putin's annual press conference  the media socially distanced with three  pcr tests behind them  the big man himself with an entrance  worthy of a blockbuster far removed on  the stage  this is a chance for mostly russian  media to ask their questions on  everything from the big picture to the  very local but despite russia's massive  troop build up on its border with  ukraine its president insisted to me he  was not threatening anyone  you have said talked a lot about  security guarantees and now we've seen  your proposals you also say you have no  intention of invading ukraine so will  you guarantee unconditionally that you  will not invade ukraine or any other  sovereign country or does that depend on  how negotiations go  uh  our actions will not depend on the  course of the negotiations but on the  unconditional compliance with russia's  security today and from a historical  perspective in this context we've made  it clear that nato's further eastward  expansion is unacceptable  i've said this many times and you  probably know this well not a single  inch to the east nato guaranteed us that  in the 1990s and you know what they  cheated us five waves of nato expansion  and there you go they're now in romania  and poland with weapon systems this is  what we're talking about it's not about  us threatening someone have we come to  the borders of the us or the uk maybe no  they came to our borders  you should not demand guarantees from us  you must give us the guarantees it's up  to you and you must do this immediately  right now  not quite right now but talks on  security are set to begin early next  year the west likely to try and buy time  russia insisting they don't drag on both  sides mired in deep mutual distrust  what is it do you think that the west  does not understand about russia or  about your intentions  sometimes it looks to me that we live in  two different worlds back in the 1990s  the ussr did everything it could to  build normal relations with the west  with the united states  you could have perhaps treated russia as  a potential ally and strengthened trust  but no instead you tried to keep  breaking us up this session was a way of  landing the message back home that  russia here is the aggrieved party  fighting off external aggressors a  question of selective memory from a keen  but distinctly amateur historian and  certainly no guarantees of peace in our  time  diana magnay sky news moscow

